hadiths[47]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1396","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man called another man at the place of Baqi, saying, ""O Abu al-Qasim!"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) looked towards him, so the man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I did not call you, I called that person (his kunyah must also have been Abu al-Qasim)."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunyah."""
"1397","Sidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that a child was born to one of us and he named him Muhammad. His people said to him, ""We will not let you keep this name; you are naming him after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" So that man carried his child on his back and brought him to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, a son has been born to me and I have named him Muhammad, but my people say, 'We will not let you do this; you are naming him after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).'"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Name him with my name, but do not use my kunyah (i.e., Abu al-Qasim), for I am al-Qasim; I distribute among you (knowledge of religion, spoils of war, etc.)."""
"1398","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The best of your names in the sight of Allah Almighty are Abdullah and Abdur-Rahman."
"1399","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` a son was born to one of us, so he named him Qasim. We said, ""We will not give you the kunya of Abu al-Qasim, nor will we cool your eyes."" He went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned this, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said that he should name his son Abdur Rahman."
"1400","‘Urwah bin Zubair and Fatimah bint Mundhir bin Zubair narrate that both of them said that Sayyidah Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her) set out (from Makkah) with the intention of migration, and she was pregnant with ‘Abdullah bin Zubair (i.e., she was expecting him). When she arrived at Quba’, Sayyiduna ‘Abdullah bin Zubair was born there. After his birth, she brought him to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) so that he (peace be upon him) could perform tahnik for him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took him from Sayyidah Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her) and seated him in his lap, then asked for a date. Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that we searched for a date for a while, then finally the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) chewed the date and put (its juice) into his mouth. The very first thing that entered ‘Abdullah’s stomach was the saliva of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Sayyidah Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her) said that after this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stroked ‘Abdullah and supplicated for him and named him ‘Abdullah. Then, when he was seven or eight years old, at the indication of Sayyiduna Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him), he came to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to pledge allegiance. When the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw him coming, he smiled. Then he took the pledge from him (for blessing, as he was a child)."
"1401","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) had a son who was ill. He (Abu Talha) was out when the boy passed away. When he returned, he asked, ""How is my child?"" (His wife) Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with her) replied, ""Now he is more at ease than before"" (this was an allusion to his death, and not a lie). Then Umm Sulaym brought him the evening meal, and he ate. After that, he had relations with Umm Sulaym. When they were finished, Umm Sulaym said, ""Go and bury the child."" In the morning, Abu Talha went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him of everything that had happened. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""Did you have relations with your wife last night?"" Abu Talha replied, ""Yes."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed, ""O Allah, bless them both."" Later, Umm Sulaym gave birth to a boy, so Abu Talha said to me, ""Take this child to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him),"" and Umm Sulaym sent some dates along with the child. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took the child and asked, ""Is there anything with him?"" The people replied, ""Dates."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took the dates, chewed them, then took them out of his mouth and put them into the child's mouth, and performed tahneek for him, and named him Abdullah."
"1402","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) that when I came to Najran, the (Ansari) people there objected to me, saying, “You recite: ‘O sister of Harun’ (__QUR_N__) (i.e., Maryam is called the sister of Harun), whereas (Sayyiduna Harun was the brother of Musa, peace be upon them) and Musa (peace be upon him) was so long before ‘Isa (peace be upon him). (So how could Maryam be the sister of Harun?)” When I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I asked him about it. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “(This is not the same Harun who was the brother of Musa.) It was the custom of Bani Isra’il (just as it is the custom of everyone now) that they would name people after the prophets and the righteous who came before.”"
"1403","`Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) says:` A son was born to me, so I brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace be upon him) named him Ibrahim and chewed a date and put it in his mouth."
"1404","Sahl bin Sa’d says that Abu Usaid’s son Mundhir, when he was born, was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed him on his thigh, and (his father) Abu Usaid was sitting. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) became occupied with something in front of him, so Abu Usaid ordered, and the child was taken off the Prophet’s thigh. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) noticed, he asked, “Where is the child?” Abu Usaid said, “O Messenger of Allah! We have taken him away.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, “What is his name?” Abu Usaid said, “Such-and-such name.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “No, his name is Mundhir.” From that day, they named him Mundhir."
"1405","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that one of Sayyiduna Umar’s (may Allah be pleased with him) daughters was named Asiyah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) changed her name to Jameelah."
"1406","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` the name of Umm al-Mu'mineen Juwayriyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) was previously Barrah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) changed her name to Juwayriyyah. He (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked that it be said that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) left the house of Barrah (the righteous wife)."
"1407","Muhammad bin Umar bin Ata says: I named my daughter Barrah, so Zainab bint Abi Salamah said that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade this name, and my name was also Barrah. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Do not praise yourselves, for Allah knows best who among you is better. The people asked: Then what should we name her? He (peace be upon him) said: Name her Zainab."
"1408","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should call grapes ""Karam,"" for ""Karam"" refers to a Muslim man."
"1409","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Wa'il bin Hujr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not call (grapes) ""karm"", rather call them ""inab"" or ""hablah""."
"1410","Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم forbade us from giving our slaves these four names: Aflah, Rabah, Yasar, and Nafi’."
"1411","´Sayyiduna Samurah bin Jundub رضي الله عنه narrates that` the Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم said: Allah Almighty loves four words the most: (Subhan Allah, Alhamdulillah, La ilaha illallah,) and (Allahu Akbar). Whichever of them one says first, it does not matter. And do not name your slave Yasar, Rabah, Najeeh (which has the same meaning as Aflah), or Aflah, because if you ask, ""Is he there?"" (i.e., Yasar or Rabah or Najeeh or Aflah), and he is not there, then it will be said, ""He is not here."" These are only four; do not add more to them for me."
"1412","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to prohibit naming with names such as Ya’la, Barakah, Aflah, Yasar, and Nafi’ and similar names. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent and did not say anything. After that, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away and he did not prohibit it. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to prohibit it, but then left it and did not prohibit it."
"1413","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should say to his slave, ""Give water to your lord,"" or ""Feed your lord,"" or ""Make ablution for your lord,"" and none of you should call another ""my lord."" Rather, say ""my master"" or ""my patron."" And none of you should say ""my slave"" or ""my slave-girl,"" but say ""my young man"" or ""my young woman."""
"1414","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was the most cheerful of all people. I had a brother who was called Abu Umair (from this it is known that it is permissible to use a kunyah for a young child or one who does not have a child). (I think Anas said that) he had been weaned. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would come and see him, he would say, ""O Abu Umair! Where is the Nughair?"" (Nughair refers to a nightingale or a small bird), and the boy used to play with it."
"1415","Sayyiduna Mughirah bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: No one asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about the Dajjal as much as I did. Finally, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Son, why are you so worried about this? He will not harm you.” I said: “People say that he will have streams of water and mountains of bread with him?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: “It is because of this that he will be disgraced in the sight of Allah, the Exalted.”"
"1416","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: The most despicable and worst name in the sight of Allah Almighty is that of the person whom people call ""Malik al-Muluk"" (King of Kings). In another narration, it is stated that there is no owner except Allah Almighty. Sufyan (i.e., Ibn Uyaynah) said that ""Malik al-Muluk"" is like ""Shahanshah"" (Emperor). And Imam Ahmad bin Hanbal said: I asked Abu Amr about the meaning of ""Akhna‘"", and he said that it means the most despicable."
"1417","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A Muslim has five rights over his Muslim brother: to return his greeting, to respond to his sneeze, to accept his invitation, to visit him when he is sick, and to accompany his funeral."
"1418","Narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A Muslim has six rights over his Muslim brother. The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What are they?"" He (peace be upon him) said: When you meet him, greet him with Salam; when he invites you, accept his invitation; when he seeks your advice, give him good advice; when he sneezes and says Alhamdulillah, respond to him (by saying Yarhamuk Allah); when he is ill, visit him; and when he dies, accompany his funeral."
"1419","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: Avoid sitting in the pathways. The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We are compelled to sit in our gatherings and talk."" So he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If you must do so, then fulfill the rights of the pathway. They asked, ""What are the rights of the pathway?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Lowering the gaze, not causing harm to anyone, responding to greetings, enjoining good, and forbidding evil."
"1420","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The rider should greet the one who is walking, the one who is walking should greet the one who is sitting, and a smaller group should greet a larger group."
"1421","Abu Burdah narrates from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, ""Peace be upon you, Abdullah bin Qais has come."" But he did not permit him to enter. Then he said, ""Peace be upon you, Abu Musa is here. Peace be upon you, this Ash'ari has come."" (First he mentioned his name, then his kunyah, then his lineage, so that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) would have no doubt.) Eventually, he returned. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Bring him back to me."" He returned and said, ""O Abu Musa, why did you leave? We were busy with work."" He said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, 'Seeking permission is three times; if permission is granted, then good, otherwise return.'"" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Bring a witness for this hadith, otherwise I will do this and that (meaning, I will punish you)."" Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him), upon hearing this, left. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""If Abu Musa finds a witness, you will find him by the pulpit in the evening; if he does not find a witness, you will not find him by the pulpit."" When Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the pulpit in the evening, Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) was present. Sayyiduna Umar said, ""O Abu Musa! What do you say, did you find a witness?"" He said, ""Yes, Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) is present."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Indeed, he is trustworthy."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Abu al-Tufail!"" (This is the kunyah of Ibn Abi Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him)), ""What does Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) say?"" Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say,"" then he supported Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, ""O son of Khattab, do not be a torment upon the companions of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) (i.e., do not trouble them)."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Glory be to Allah! When I heard a hadith, I thought it better to verify it."" (And my intention was never, God forbid, to trouble the companions of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), nor did I mean that Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) was lying.)"
"1422","`Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You have permission to come to me in such a way that the curtain is lifted and you can also listen to my conversation, until I stop you."
"1423","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked, ""Who is it?"" I replied, ""It is I."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""'It is I, it is I.'"" In another narration, it is as if the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked saying ""It is I."""
"1424","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man peeped through a hole in the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had an iron tool (comb) in his hand, with which he was scratching his head. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw him, he said: “If I had known that you were looking at me, I would have poked your eye.” And the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Permission (to enter) has been prescribed only to protect the eye (i.e., from peeping into someone else’s house, and this is forbidden).”"
"1425","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: If someone peeps into your house without your permission, and then you throw a pebble at him and his eye is injured, there will be no sin upon you."
"1426","'Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that' I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about an accidental glance, so he (peace be upon him) commanded me to turn my gaze away."
"1427","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Waqid Al-Laithi (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting in the mosque and people were with him, when three men came. Two of them came straight to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and one went away. Of the two who came, one found a vacant spot in the gathering and sat there, and the other sat behind the people, and the third turned away and left. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: ""Shall I not tell you about these three men? One sought refuge with Allah, so Allah gave him refuge; the second felt shy (to push in among the people), so Allah was shy with him; and the third turned away, so Allah turned away from him."""
"1428","´Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: None of you should make his brother get up from his place and then sit there himself, but rather spread out and make room. In another narration, it is mentioned that I asked: Is this command for the day of Jumu'ah? He (peace be upon him) said: Whether it is Jumu'ah or any other day. And if someone would stand up for Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), he would not sit in that place (even though it is permissible to sit with his consent, but this was caution lest he might be displeased in his heart)."
"1429","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When any one of you stands up from a gathering (for some need), (and in the narration of Abu Awanah: whoever stands up), then returns, he is more entitled to that place."
"1430","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When you are three people, then two of you should not converse privately excluding the third person, until more people join you. This is because (the third person) will be grieved. (It is possible that he may become suspicious of the two.)"
"1431","Siyar says that I was walking with Thabit Banani, he passed by some children and greeted them with salam and narrated a hadith that he was walking with Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), they passed by some children and greeted them with salam, and Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated a hadith that he was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), they passed by some children and he (peace and blessings be upon him) greeted them with salam."
"1432","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not initiate the greeting of salam to the Jews and Christians, and when you meet any of them on the road, force him to the narrowest part of it."
"1433","‘Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that a group of Jews greeted the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and said, “As-saam ‘alaikum, O Abu al-Qasim!” (meaning: O Abu al-Qasim, death be upon you). The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied, “Wa ‘alaikum.” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) became angry and said, “Did you not hear what they said?” The Prophet (peace be upon him) replied, “I heard it and I responded to them, and the supplication we make against them is accepted, but their supplication is not accepted.” (And so it happened that death befell the Jews—they died and were killed.)"
"1434","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the pure wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to go at night to those places (for relieving themselves) which were outside of Madinah, and they were open and clear places. And Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that you should keep your women in seclusion (veil). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not command veiling. Once, Umm al-Mu'mineen Sawda bint Zam‘a (may Allah be pleased with her) went out at night at the time of ‘Isha, and she was a tall woman. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) called out to her and said, ""O Sawda bint Zam‘a! We have recognized you."" And he did this so that the command of veiling would be revealed. Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said, then Allah Almighty revealed the command of veiling."
"1435","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: When the command of veiling was revealed to us, after that, Sawda (may Allah be pleased with her) went out to relieve herself, and she was a heavy woman, who stood out among all women in her stoutness, and whoever knew her could not fail to recognize her (that is, he would recognize her). So, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) saw her and said, “O Sawda! By Allah, you cannot hide yourself from us, so consider how you go out.” Hearing this, she returned, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was eating dinner in my house, and there was a bone in his hand. At that moment, Sawda came and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I went out, and Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said such and such to me.” Immediately, the state of revelation came upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), then that state passed, and the bone was still in his hand, he had not put it down. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “You have been permitted to go out for your needs.”"
"1436","Lady Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with both of them) says: Zubair bin Al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him) married me (who was the cousin of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him), and he had no wealth, nor any slave, nor anything else except for a horse. I used to graze his horse and do all the work for the horse and train it, and I would also crush date stones for his camel, graze it, give it water, sew the bucket, and knead the flour. But I could not bake bread well, so the Ansari women neighbors would bake my bread, and they were very loving women. Asma said: I used to carry date stones on my head from the land of Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him), which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had given him as a grant, and that land was two miles from Madinah. (A mile is six thousand handspans, a handspan is twenty-four fingers, a finger is six barley grains, and a farsakh is three miles.) One day, I was bringing date stones from there when on the way I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and several of his companions. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called me and then made a sound to make the camel kneel so that I could ride behind him. I felt shy and modest. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Allah, carrying the load of date stones on your head is harder than riding with me."" (Meaning, you endure such a burden, so why not ride with me?) Lady Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Later, Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) gave me a servant, and she started doing all the work for the horse, as if he had set me free."
"1437","Umm al-Mu'mineen Safiyyah bint Huyayy (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was in i'tikaf. I came to visit him at night. I spoke with him, then when I stood up to return, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also stood up with me to see me off, and my house was in the dwelling of Usamah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him). On the way, two men from the Ansar met us. When they saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), they began to walk quickly. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Wait, this is Safiyyah bint Huyayy."" Both of them said, ""Subhan Allah, O Messenger of Allah!"" (meaning, could we ever think ill of you?) The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Satan flows through the human body like blood, and I feared that he might cast an evil thought into your hearts (and thus you would be ruined because of it)."""
"1438","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Beware! No man should stay with a married woman at night except if she is accompanied by her husband or a mahram."
"1439","Narrated from Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Avoid going to women. An Ansari man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What about the husband's brother?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""The husband's brother is death."" (Meaning, the real danger is from the husband's brother.) Sayyiduna Laith bin Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say that in the hadith where it is mentioned that the husband's brother is death, it refers to the husband's relatives and close ones, such as the husband's brother or his paternal cousin (all those relatives of the husband with whom marriage is permissible for the woman are included among the husband's brothers, and she should observe veiling from them, except for the husband's father, grandfather, or his son, as they are mahram and there is no need to observe veiling from them)."
"1440","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) that some people from Banu Hashim went to Asma bint Umais, and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) also went, and at that time Asma was married to Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). They saw them and disliked their coming. Then it was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said, ""I have not seen anything wrong."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Allah has purified Asma from any evil act."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on the pulpit and said, ""From today, no man should enter the house of a woman whose husband is absent (i.e., not at home), except that he brings one or two men with him."" (By this he meant his own men, about whom it is impossible to think that they would go to a woman of ill character.)"
"1441","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that a mukhannath (effeminate man) used to come to the wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and they considered him among those who have no interest in women (and in the Qur’an, it is permitted for such people to appear before women). One day, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to one of his wives, and he (the mukhannath) was describing a woman, saying: “When she comes forward, she comes with four folds, and when she turns her back, eight folds become visible.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “He recognizes those who are here (i.e., he likes and distinguishes the beauty and ugliness of women); do not let him come to you.” (Sayyida Aisha says) So they stopped him from coming."
"1442","`Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` a house in Madinah caught fire at night. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was informed, he said: This fire is your enemy, so when you go to sleep, extinguish it."
